* LTC6252 High-Speed Amplifier -- Non-Inverting Gain of 2 (+/-5V supplies)
* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Supplies
V1 VCC 0 DC 5
V2 VEE 0 DC -5

* Input: 1 V amplitude sine at 10 MHz (AC magnitude 1 for optional .ac run)
Vin IN 0 SINE(0 1 10MEG) AC 1

* Genuine LTC6252 macromodel (pin order: +IN -IN V+ V- OUT)
XU1 IN FB VCC VEE OUT LTC6252
.include LTC6252.sub

* Non-inverting gain = 1 + Rf/Rg = 1 + 1k/1k = 2 V/V (6.02 dB)
Rf OUT FB 1k
Rg FB 0 1k

* Supply decoupling
Cvcc VCC 0 1u
Cvee VEE 0 1u

* Load
RL OUT 0 1k

* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Transient analysis: 20 cycles of 10 MHz, measure gain over last cycles
.tran 0 2u 0 100p

* Measurements (steady-state window: 1.8us to 2.0us = last 2 cycles)
.meas TRAN vin_pp  PP V(IN)  FROM=1.8u TO=2.0u
.meas TRAN vout_pp PP V(OUT) FROM=1.8u TO=2.0u
.meas TRAN gain    PARAM vout_pp/vin_pp
.meas TRAN gain_db PARAM 20*log10(vout_pp/vin_pp)

* Optional small-signal frequency response (uncomment to use)
* .ac dec 100 10k 1G

.options plotwinsize=0
.end
